# ffmpeg — NEVER commit or ship a binary (Phase 53).
#
# ffmpeg is LGPL-2.1, and GPL when built --enable-gpl. Committing one
# here, or letting one reach a release artifact, turns this project into
# a *distributor* of it: that carries a permanent per-release obligation
# to ship its source or a written offer and to let users relink, and
# `deny.toml` would have to be reopened to admit LGPL at all.
#
# The feature is deliberately built around a binary the USER installs
# and points us at (`crates/freally-mergeview/src/ffmpeg.rs`), because
# invoking one at arms length distributes nothing. It is opt-in and
# absent by default. These rules exist so a stray download in the tree
# can never quietly undo that.
ffmpeg
ffmpeg.exe
ffprobe
ffprobe.exe
ffplay
ffplay.exe
**/ffmpeg-*/
avcodec-*.dll
avformat-*.dll
avutil-*.dll
avdevice-*.dll
avfilter-*.dll
swresample-*.dll
swscale-*.dll
postproc-*.dll
libav*.so*
libsw*.so*
libav*.dylib
libsw*.dylib

# Same reasoning as docs/SECURITY_BACKLOG.md above: this repo is public,
# and the review backlog names unfixed issues (including a local
# root-privilege escalation) with enough detail to act on. Publishing it
# would hand users' attackers a worked example before the fix ships.
REVIEW-BACKLOG.md

# Build handoff notes. Working documents between build sessions: they
# quote unfixed findings, name file/line targets, and describe attacks
# in enough detail to reproduce them. Same public-repo reasoning as
# REVIEW-BACKLOG.md above.
/BUILD3-HANDOFF.md
/BUILD3-CLOSEOUT-TASKS.md
/BUILD4-HANDOFF.md
/TONIGHT-TASKS.md

